{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"lovesick-missing-andeancat","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Context\n\nThe fixture-admission runner (`src/rebar/llm/evals/fixture_admission.py`, epic REB-693 / 67aa) SCOPES OUT container criteria (G3/G4/decomp-shape) as `container-material-unrecoverable`: the replay corpus (`src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py`) persists a review's children as bare ticket-id STRINGS only (`_child_ids`), with no per-child title/description. But the LIVE plan-review container finder reads each child's full title/description at review time (`context_assembly.py` fetches every child via `show_ticket`), and G3's coverage-discharge cannot fire on a title-only roster (`container_stage.py`). So a container case rehydrated from the corpus would run the finder over an IMPOVERISHED roster — an admit/drift verdict UNFAITHFUL to history. `material_fingerprint` hashes children by id only (`material_diff.py`), so it cannot detect the loss.\n\n## Approach\n\nExtend the corpus sidecar row to persist per-child at-review `{canonical_id, title, description}` (reconstruct each child's title+description from its OWN event history at `review_ts`, reusing the `_reconstruct_material` machinery already used for the parent description), and rehydrate those into the `{ticket_id, title, description}` records the container finder consumes. When a child's at-review material is unrecoverable, withhold that case to drift as unrecoverable rather than running the finder over a degraded roster. Then REMOVE the container scope-out guard in `fixture_admission.run_admission` and re-run a live admission over G3/G4/decomp-shape to mint faithful specs.\n\n## Scope\n\n`corpus.py` (per-child material reconstruction + persistence), `fixture_admission.py` (drop the container scope-out once corpus is faithful), the container eval specs re-minted by a live run.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The corpus sidecar row persists per-child `{canonical_id, title, description}` reconstructed at `review_ts`; a unit test over synthetic child histories asserts the reconstructed title/description match the child's state as of the review.\n- [ ] The admission runner rehydrates container children WITH title/description and dispatches G3/G4 to the finder (no longer withheld as container-material-unrecoverable); a held-out test asserts a container must-fire case reproduces over the faithful roster.\n- [ ] A child whose at-review material is unrecoverable withholds that case to drift as unrecoverable (not a degraded-roster finder call).\n- [ ] A live admission run mints faithful G3/G4 specs; ledger records the spend ≤ cap.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n`make lint`/`make typecheck`/`make test` pass; container specs re-minted faithfully.","id":"2340-d9a9-2e49-4c18","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Persist per-child at-review material so container criteria (G3/G4) admit faithfully"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788489907724048001,"uuid":"f1f765d6-4983-4a86-9307-8d7f629dff11"}